  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Acidic character <math><mi>&#945;</mi></math> stability of conjugate base (anion)<br /><br />Stability of anion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math><br /><br />Hence greater the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> effect greater will be the acidity<br /><br />Order of -I-effect <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>CN</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>Cl</mi></math> Hence, order of acidity &nbsp;will be<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>NCH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>COOH</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>NC</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>COOH</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>FCH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>COOH</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>Cl</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>COOH</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p>"
